Z||000009||AusFiero||07-29-2001||07:56 AM||||Ok heres a tip from my days in automotive graphics design Smooth. Used to do graphics and decal, striping designs for Holden, Toyota and Ford at a company I worked for.  <P>OOPS stuffed the below info up. Fixed now<P>To make a car look taller or lower you use 2 tone. Dark over light makes a car look lower. Light over dark makes the roofline look taller. Colour wise light colours give the illusion of size. Light colours with darker sill,  lower bumper areas look larger than they are. So it is bigger with the lights on afterall   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A><p>[This message has been edited by AusFiero (edited 07-29-2001).]||202.139.20.3||reg||1
